From: OpenIPC device support <openipc@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] sta_cfg: bound-check keyIdx in the SECURITY_DISABLED branch

RT_CMD_STA_IOCTL_SECURITY_DISABLED is taken straight from the WEXT
SIOCSIWENCODEEXT request, but the key index is never validated against
the key table before it is used to index pAd->SharedKey[BSS0][keyIdx].

In STA mode that table is declared as

    CIPHER_KEY SharedKey[1][4];   /* include/rtmp.h */
    /* STA always use SharedKey[BSS0][0..3] */

so indices 4 and 5 address past the end of the array. The writes

    pAd->SharedKey[BSS0][keyIdx].KeyLen = 0;
    pAd->SharedKey[BSS0][keyIdx].CipherAlg = CIPHER_NONE;
    NdisZeroMemory(&pAd->SharedKey[BSS0][keyIdx], sizeof(CIPHER_KEY));

then corrupt the adapter fields that follow SharedKey, and
AsicRemoveSharedKeyEntry() trips its ASSERT(KeyIdx < 4).

The sibling (non-disabled) branch below already performs exactly this
check, so mirror it here. This is reachable from unprivileged ioctl
input and was observed in the field with keyIdx reaching 4 and 5.

--- a/sta/sta_cfg.c
+++ b/sta/sta_cfg.c
@@ -8801,6 +8801,9 @@
     if (pIoctlSec->flags == RT_CMD_STA_IOCTL_SECURITY_DISABLED)
     {
         keyIdx = pIoctlSec->KeyIdx; /*(encoding->flags & IW_ENCODE_INDEX) - 1; */
+        if ((keyIdx < 0) || (keyIdx >= NR_WEP_KEYS))
+            return NDIS_STATUS_FAILURE;
+
         /* set BSSID wcid entry of the Pair-wise Key table as no-security mode */
 	    AsicRemovePairwiseKeyEntry(pAd, BSSID_WCID);
         pAd->SharedKey[BSS0][keyIdx].KeyLen = 0;
